3690","L7-3750","L7-3810","L7-4010","L7-4051","L7-4107","L7-4314","L7-4339","L7-4725","L7-4733","L7-4811","L7-4849","L7-4930","L7-5074","L7-5224","L7-5255","L7-5349","L7-5476","L7-5549","L7-5550","L7-5592","L7-5614"],"chemin":{"hsk":13,"lire":13},"sens":{"statut":"relu","glose":"enfant, fils, suffixe de nom","acceptions":[]},"exemples":[{"zh":"桌子上有一本书。","pinyin":"Zhuōzi shang yǒu yī běn shū.","fr":"Il y a un livre sur la table.","statut":"relu"}],"origine":{"statut":"relu","etiquette":"atteste","fr":"Sur les os oraculaires et les bronzes, 子 dessine un nourrisson : une grosse tête, deux bras ouverts, le bas du corps réduit à un seul trait, comme pris dans un lange. Le sens premier, « enfant », a donné « fils », puis un titre de respect pour les maîtres, comme dans Kongzi, Confucius. Prononcé zi, sans ton, il sert aussi de suffixe à de nombreux noms, comme 日子, les jours.","en":"On oracle bones and bronzes, 子 draws an infant: a large head, two open arms, and the lower body reduced to a single stroke, as if wrapped in swaddling. Its first meaning, “child”, gave “son”, then a title of respect for masters, as in Kongzi, Confucius. Pronounced zi with no tone, it is also a suffix found in many nouns, such as 日子, days.","roles":{}}},"紫":{"c":"紫","pinyin":"zǐ","lectures":["zǐ"],"niveau":5,"decomposition":{"norme":"GF 0014-2009","parts":["止","匕","糸"],"sources":["cjk-decomp"]},"mots":["L5-1058"],"chemin":{},"sens":{"statut":"relu","glose":"violet, pourpre","acceptions":[{"categorie":"Adj","fr":"violet, pourpre"}]},"exemples":[{"zh":"她穿了一条紫色的裙子。","pinyin":"Tā chuān le yī tiáo zǐsè de qúnzi.","fr":"Elle porte une jupe violette.","statut":"relu"}],"origine":null},"字":{"c":"字","pinyin":"zì","lectures":["zì"],"niveau":1,"decomposition":{"norme":"GF 0014-2009","parts":["宀","子"],"sources":["cjk-decomp"]},"mots":["L1-0137","L1-0245","L1-0488","L2-0502","L2-0754","L3-0764","L4-0989","L5-0584","L6-0741","L6-0898","L6-0899","L7-0490","L7-0670","L7-1047","L7-2000","L7-2147","L7-2539","L7-3697","L7-5576","L7-5577","L7-5578","L7-5579"],"chemin":{"hsk":141,"lire":127},"sens":{"statut":"relu","glose":"caractère, mot, écriture","acceptions":[]},"exemples":[{"zh":"这个字怎么读？","pinyin":"Zhège zì zěnme dú?","fr":"Comment se lit ce caractère ?","statut":"relu"},{"zh":"他的字很好看。","pinyin":"Tā de zì hěn hǎokàn.","fr":"Il a une belle écriture.","statut":"relu"}],"origine":{"statut":"relu","etiquette":"atteste","fr":"Sur les bronzes, 字 montre un enfant 子 sous le toit d'une maison 宀. Le Shuowen jiezi y lit le sens de mettre au monde et d'élever, et donne aussi 子 zǐ pour le son, proche de zì. De la famille qui s'agrandit, le sens a glissé vers les caractères écrits, qui en engendrent d'autres à leur tour.","en":"On bronzes, 字 shows a child 子 under the roof of a house 宀. The Shuowen jiezi reads it as giving birth and raising, and also takes 子 zǐ for the sound, close to zì. From a growing family, the meaning moved to written characters, which breed new ones in turn.","roles":{"宀":"sens","子":"son"}}},"自":{"c":"自","pinyin":"zì","lectures":["zì"],"niveau":2,"decomposition":{"norme":"GF 0014-2009","parts":[],"sources":[]},"mots":["L2-0100","L2-0335","L2-0751","L2-0752","L2-0753","L3-0236","L3-0564","L3-0958","L3-0959","L3-0960","L3-0961","L3-0962","L3-0963","L4-0200","L4-0987","L4-0988","L5-1059","L5-1060","L5-1061","L6-1112","L6-1113","L6-1114","L6-1115","L6-1116","L7-0299","L7-0559","L7-0942","L7-3348","L7-3552","L7-3879","L7-3911","L7-4895","L7-5551","L7-5552","L7-5553","L7-5554","L7-5555","L7-5556","L7-5557","L7-5558","L7-5559","L7-5560","L7-5561","L7-5562","L7-5563","L7-5564","L7-5565","L7-5566","L7-5567","L7-5568","L7-5569","L7-5570","L7-5571","L7-5572","L7-5573","L7-5574","L7-5575"],"chemin":{"hsk":174},"sens":{"statut":"relu","glose":"soi-même ; depuis","acceptions":[{"categorie":"Pron","fr":"soi-même, de soi"},{"categorie":"Prep","fr":"depuis, à partir de"}]},"exemples":[{"zh":"我自己来。","pinyin":"Wǒ zìjǐ lái.","fr":"Je m'en occupe moi-même.","statut":"relu"}],"origine"